  "verdict": "As specified (buffers + structure combined), structural features do NOT help (-0.039 vs the 0.375 baseline) -- the combined classifier is worse, not just unchanged. A diagnostic run using ONLY the 7 structural features (no buffers) scored 0.454 macro-F1 -- higher than both baseline (0.375) and the combined 13-feature model (0.336). So plan structure does carry real signal on its own; concatenating it onto the buffer features and handing 13 features to a random forest with only 20 training rows per leave-one-query-out fold apparently dilutes rather than adds -- consistent with 21 queries being too few to support a wider feature set, not with structure being uninformative."
